WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
[ Indistinct conversations ]

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've been here for like
seven hours already.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.704 line:92%
-I've been here for five hours.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who among us knows
the purpose of this meeting?

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the host did not say,
Lord Black Thought.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, alas, my little birds
have told me nothing.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, regrettably,
one of my little birds

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
decided to drop a deuce
upon my tunic.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.164 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You may be seated.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:40.573
I have summoned this meeting of
the regular-sized council

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.644 size:81% position:41%
to answer one question
and one question only.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:46.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Laurel, My Lord.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.781 line:92%
An answer to your question.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.182 line:92%
I once thought it to be yanny,

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
but in point of fact,
the voice does say "Laurel."

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:59.125
-I seek the answer to one
question and one question only.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:07.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
How long must we [bleep]
wait for "Game of Thrones"?!

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.235 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-The TV show, My Lord?

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.906
-"Game of Thrones" is no mere
TV show, Lord Black Thought.

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a way of life.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.110 size:84% position:42%
A hallowed epic cruelly
torn from our bosoms

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
by a production hiatus
most vile.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.282 line:92%
Winter has come and gone.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then winter
has come and gone again.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:30.090 size:84% position:42%
And now 'tis spring,
and one thing is clear.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.725 line:92%
Shorts weather is coming.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.562 line:92%
So, I shall ask one more time.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
When will
"Game of Thrones" return?

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've had the same question,
My Lord.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.736
For two years, I've had nothing
to watch, nothing to binge,

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
nothing to amuse me

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:51.611 line:92%
but the memory of my balls.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.414 line:92%
-I got a question for you.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why am I paying more for
HBO still? Why?

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The wait, indeed,
has been long.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
I myself have been forced
to watch...broadcast.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And does anyone like
"Young Sheldon?"

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:11.898 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Does anyone like it?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, genuinely like it,
for real?

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is there no one
who can answer my question?

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.571 line:92%
-Might I suggest, My Lord,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
perhaps we do not want
"Game of Thrones" to return.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What?
[ Laughs ]

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.215 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Not want it to return?

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-What is this blasphemy?

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, he is cray, My Lord.
The man is cray-cray.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shame!
-Shame!

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:41.661
-No! My Lord, it is simply that
if the show does not return,

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:45.365 line:92%
then it cannot come to an end.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.368 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-He's got a good point.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's actually a pretty good
point right there.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.638 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It is true, My Lord.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
The show cannot end
if it does not return.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:58.044
It would remain forever in
the realm of what still may be.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:02.248
-Lord Higbones, all great shows
must come to an end.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:05.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
A great show does not overstay
it's welcome.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:11.925
"Game of Thrones" must end,
but in order for it to end,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:15.295 size:81% position:41% line:92%
it must [bleep] begin.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.797 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
When will it --

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Silence!

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:28.107 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Patience, My Lord.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:31.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your temper will not hasten
the end you seek.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.080 size:84% position:42% line:92%
The premiere is coming.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:39.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
But until then,
we mustn't lose our heads.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you get it?
-No.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Mustn't lose our heads."
[ Laughs ]

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.236 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You get it?

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We mustn't lose our heads."
[ Laughs ]

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's good, isn't it, that?
Funny.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.575 line:92%
-I don't -- I don't get it.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:08.114
-No matter, Higbones.
We are no closer to the answer.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:11.684 line:92%
When will "Game of Thrones" --

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-April 14th.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.057 line:92%
-What's that you say, good man?

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:23.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The final season premieres
April 14th.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But have no fear.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:28.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
After the show ends,
there will still be books.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:33.273
-Mysterious stranger, how do we
know that you speak the truth?

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.843 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Trust me. I know a guy.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:44.550 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-The premiere is coming.

